"sawtooth" <bagofholding@gmail.com> wrote:

> 
> defklown wrote:
>> When putting on armor, the enchantment auto-identifies, but this isn't
>> the case with weapons. Is there a way to tell what enchantment a weapon
>> has without reading a scroll of identify?
> 
> Armor auto-id's because you can see the effect it has on your total AC.
>  This is not the case for weapons.  You just can't easily tell the
> enchantment  a weapon has just by wielding it.  As was mentioned
> already shops are the way to id weapon enchantments without a scroll of
> id.  I suppose the other way is to engrave with an edged weapon until
> you get it to -3. :)  Once you can't engrave anymore then you know the
> enchantment!
> 
That doesn't work for all weapons, not even all edged weapons.

Less drastically, you could just cancel it to get the enchantment to  a 
known +0. Or enchant it more until it vibrates and then you'll have a 
pretty good idea of the enchantment.


